---
components: ["ConfirmModal"]
description: ConfirmModal is a preset over Modal for are-you-sure decisions, with danger, warning, and info kinds and an optional type-to-confirm phrase.
---

## Basic

Ask the user to confirm or cancel an action. `heading` sets the modal title, and `confirmText`/`cancelText` label the two footer buttons. Listen for `on:confirm` and `on:cancel` to react to the choice; the modal closes itself in both cases. For anything beyond a yes/no decision, use [Modal](/components/Modal) directly.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/ConfirmModal" />

## Kinds

Set `kind` to match the severity of the action. The default is `"danger"`.

### Danger

Use `kind="danger"` for destructive, irreversible actions. The confirm button uses Modal's danger styling, and the cancel button receives focus first so a stray keypress can't confirm by accident.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/DangerConfirmModal" />

### Warning

Use `kind="warning"` for actions that need attention but aren't destructive. The modal switches to Modal's alert mode and shows a warning icon next to the heading.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/WarningConfirmModal" />

### Info

Use `kind="info"` for plain confirmations with no danger or warning styling.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/InfoConfirmModal" />

## Type to confirm

Set `confirmationPhrase` to require the user to type an exact phrase before the confirm button is enabled. `confirmationLabel` controls the input's label; `{phrase}` is replaced with `confirmationPhrase`.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/ConfirmModalTypeToConfirm" />

## Async confirm

Pass the work to `onConfirm`. While the promise it returns is pending, the confirm button shows `loadingDescription`, and cancel, Escape and outside clicks are blocked. When it resolves, the modal dispatches `confirm` and closes. When it rejects, the modal stays open and shows the error's message, or `errorText`.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/ConfirmModalAsyncConfirm" />

### Manual loading

To drive the state yourself, set `loading` while the action runs and `closeOnConfirm={false}`, and close the modal when it finishes.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/ConfirmModalLoading" />

## Custom body

Use the default slot to add richer content below the confirmation prompt, such as a list of the items an action will affect.

<FileSource src="/framed/ConfirmModal/ConfirmModalCustomBody" />

## Events

### Confirm

`on:confirm` fires when the confirm button is clicked (or activated via <DocKbd label="Enter" />) and, when `confirmationPhrase` is set, the typed phrase matches. It carries no detail.

```svelte
<ConfirmModal bind:open heading="Delete this item?" on:confirm={handleDelete}>
```

### Cancel

`on:cancel` fires when the user backs out, either through the header close button or the footer cancel button. `event.detail.trigger` is `"close-button"` or `"cancel-button"`.

```svelte
<ConfirmModal
  bind:open
  heading="Delete this item?"
  on:cancel={(e) => console.log(e.detail.trigger)}
>
```

### Open, close, and transition end

`on:open`, `on:close`, and `on:transitionend` forward the underlying [Modal](/components/Modal#events) events unchanged.
